Enhancement: Reduce memory usage when backing up directories with many entries

Backing up a directory that directly contains a very large number of entries
used about a kilobyte of memory per entry. A directory of a million files needed
over a gigabyte, enough for a memory-limited host to kill the backup.

Restic now uses considerably less memory for such directories: a directory of a
million entries peaks at 773 MB instead of 1248 MB. The snapshots created are
unchanged.

